<title>AUSTRALIA: Murdoch sees Packer winning from media probe.</title>
<headline>Murdoch sees Packer winning from media probe.</headline>
<dateline>BRISBANE 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>News Corp Ltd Chief Executive and Chairman Rupert Murdoch said on Thursday the Australian government's investigation into cross-media ownership rules would probably benefit media mogul Kerry Packer.</p>
<p>Packer controls Publishing and Broadcasting Ltd, which owns the top-rating Nine Network and about 15 percent of John Fairfax Holdings Ltd.</p>
<p>&quot;It'll probably turn out the way Mr Packer wants it,&quot; Murdoch told reporters after a luncheon meeting with Queensland state Premier Rob Borbidge.</p>
</text>
